"Upstream real sample" and records every normalization/extraction step as a
derivation. CC BY 4.0 permits sharing, adaptation, commercial, and hosted-service
use without field-of-use restrictions, subject to attribution, a license link,
and indication of modifications. It requires no click-through acceptance or token.

License boundaries
------------------

* This notice covers only the starter media identified above. It does not change
  the NPA source-code license, the Cosmos Transfer source-code license, or any
  model/checkpoint license.
* Cosmos Transfer source code is pinned separately and built under Apache-2.0.
  Its model weights are fetched at runtime under the NVIDIA Open Model License.
* The Cosmos repository's example media is excluded: its source-code license is
  not an asset-level media grant and its files do not uniformly establish
  real-capture provenance. See
  npa/docker/workbench/cosmos2-transfer/REDISTRIBUTION.md.
* A user-supplied local or S3 video remains the user's responsibility. NPA records
  it as "User-supplied input" and does not infer an authenticity or license claim.

Native EVG live-test photograph
------------------------------

The EVG live-test harness fetches scikit-image's camera photograph at preparation
time, verifies its SHA-256 before staging, and writes fixture-source.json beside
the input directory. The image is not bundled in this repository or any image.

